00:39:06.595 --> 00:39:08.763
Sweeney's paranoid.
He thinks Danny stole from him

764
00:39:08.764 --> 00:39:10.848
but he didn't.
but it doesn't matter.

765
00:39:10.849 --> 00:39:12.767
Sweeney told
the bartender at the 596

766
00:39:12.768 --> 00:39:14.185
he's gonna put a bullet in Danny

767
00:39:14.186 --> 00:39:15.478
I don't get him out
of the Kitchen.

768
00:39:15.479 --> 00:39:17.855
Let me be clear
on what you're asking me.

769
00:39:17.856 --> 00:39:19.356
You want me to arrest your son?

770
00:39:19.357 --> 00:39:21.275
No. I can position that.

771
00:39:21.276 --> 00:39:23.235
What I need from you is
to use your influence

772
00:39:23.236 --> 00:39:24.904
with the authorities
to get him out of town.

773
00:39:24.905 --> 00:39:27.031
You're asking me
to use federal pull

774
00:39:27.032 --> 00:39:30.201
to ship your kid to a safe house
disguised as a clinic?

775
00:39:30.202 --> 00:39:32.244
Yeah. won't look good if the son

776
00:39:32.245 --> 00:39:34.325
of one of your informants
turns up in the East River.

777
00:39:35.665 --> 00:39:37.374
What do I get?

778
00:39:37.375 --> 00:39:40.086
I think there's a connection
between Sweeney. Castellano.

779
00:39:40.087 --> 00:39:42.171
and that fire
at the Starship disco.

780
00:39:42.172 --> 00:39:43.714
Got any proof?

781
00:39:43.715 --> 00:39:46.718
I'm workin' on it.
But not if I'm burying my kid.

782
00:39:47.886 --> 00:39:51.138
Location I can't promise.
but I'll see what I can do.

783
00:39:51.139 --> 00:39:53.683
You fuck me on this.
I'll let the kid rot.

784
00:39:54.935 --> 00:39:56.310
I owe you.

785
00:39:56.311 --> 00:39:57.812
Yeah. you do.

786
00:39:57.813 --> 00:40:00.232
[rock music playing]

787
00:40:02.818 --> 00:40:04.193
You're too fucking
trustin'. Jimmy.

788
00:40:04.194 --> 00:40:05.194
Fuck off.

789
00:40:08.949 --> 00:40:11.534
Problem is. you put
Sweeney on a pedestal.

790
00:40:11.535 --> 00:40:14.662
We all did. but now we know
he don't fuckin' belong there.

791
00:40:14.663 --> 00:40:16.080
What are you.
a fuckin' shrink now?

792
00:40:16.081 --> 00:40:17.748
Well. you ain't gotta be
a fuckin' shrink. Jimmy.

793
00:40:17.749 --> 00:40:20.626
Any idiot can see that this
motherfucker is out for himself.

794
00:40:20.627 --> 00:40:22.753
I just can't believe
I couldn't see it before.

795
00:40:22.754 --> 00:40:24.965
But now. we got to accept it.

796
00:40:27.008 --> 00:40:28.968
Look. brother. I get it.

797
00:40:28.969 --> 00:40:30.512
Right. the guy's done
a lot for you.

798
00:40:31.555 --> 00:40:33.722
After what happened with
your mother. taking you in.

799
00:40:33.723 --> 00:40:35.558
putting a roof over your head.
that's not nothing.

800
00:40:35.559 --> 00:40:37.879
And what? I'm not supposed
to be fuckin' grateful for that?

801
00:40:39.312 --> 00:40:41.105
Sure.

802
00:40:41.106 --> 00:40:43.232
But understand it
for what it is.

803
00:40:43.233 --> 00:40:45.025
He has your loyalty. right?

804
00:40:45.026 --> 00:40:47.111
You would die for
that motherfucker. I know you.

805
00:40:47.112 --> 00:40:49.196
You think
he'd say the same for you?

806
00:40:49.197 --> 00:40:51.366
He wouldn't. and he never will.

807
00:40:52.284 --> 00:40:53.617
-I can't believe that.
-Jimmy.

808
00:40:53.618 --> 00:40:55.202
the guy showed us who he is.

809
00:40:55.203 --> 00:40:57.872
He's a fuckin' criminal.
through and through.

810
00:40:57.873 --> 00:41:01.041
He pretends he's some fancy
fuckin' do-gooder. you know.

811
00:41:01.042 --> 00:41:03.669
walking around in his suits
and bowin' to old ladies.

812
00:41:03.670 --> 00:41:05.421
givin' his speeches
about the neighborhood.

813
00:41:05.422 --> 00:41:06.797
telling everybody
and their mother.

814
00:41:06.798 --> 00:41:08.382
oh. no. we don't sell narcotics.

815
00:41:08.383 --> 00:41:10.384
No. that's not in our streets.
that's a dirty business.

816
00:41:10.385 --> 00:41:12.094
But then what does he do?

817
00:41:12.095 --> 00:41:14.096
He sells our product
and uses the money for himself.

818
00:41:14.097 --> 00:41:16.057
it makes me fuckin' sick!

819
00:41:17.100 --> 00:41:19.059
I just can't believe
he lied to my fuckin' face.

820
00:41:19.060 --> 00:41:21.228
Right. but he did.

821
00:41:21.229 --> 00:41:22.646
Jimmy. this is
the same motherfucker

822
00:41:22.647 --> 00:41:24.315
that killed Davey O'Brien.

823
00:41:24.316 --> 00:41:26.150
and he wanted you to shoot me.

824
00:41:26.151 --> 00:41:27.277
And you know what?

825
00:41:29.029 --> 00:41:30.613
I haven't heard shit about Pat

826
00:41:30.614 --> 00:41:32.073
since he said
he was lookin' into it.

827
00:41:33.575 --> 00:41:35.201
I'm just saying.

828
00:41:35.202 --> 00:41:37.036
now we know
that this motherfucker

829
00:41:37.037 --> 00:41:38.371
ain't one of us.

830
00:41:41.124 --> 00:41:43.334
So what am I supposed to do?

831
00:41:43.335 --> 00:41:44.461
Hmm?

832
00:41:46.379 --> 00:41:48.048
You know. what if we're wrong?

833
00:41:49.257 --> 00:41:51.258
What if he didn't sell the coke?
He just... He just donated

834
00:41:51.259 --> 00:41:52.927
that money from his...
from his savings.

835
00:41:52.928 --> 00:41:54.220
[scoffs]

836
00:41:54.221 --> 00:41:56.055
Right...

837
00:41:56.056 --> 00:41:57.976
and I hear there's
a bridge in Brooklyn for sale.

838
00:42:02.312 --> 00:42:05.482
You know. you got a heart
of fuckin' gold. Jimmy.

839
00:42:06.858 --> 00:42:09.361
Don't ever lose that. Please.

840
00:42:10.654 --> 00:42:12.029
But don't give it
to a motherfucker

841
00:42:12.030 --> 00:42:13.490
who don't deserve it either.

842
00:42:16.618 --> 00:42:18.202
Where're you going?

843
00:42:18.203 --> 00:42:19.995
I'm going
to that fuckin' dinner.

844
00:42:19.996 --> 00:42:21.497
And I'm gonna make him
tell me the fuckin' truth.

845
00:42:21.498 --> 00:42:22.540
[loud slam]

846
00:42:48.775 --> 00:42:51.193
[Glenn]
Jacob's Biscuits.

847
00:42:51.194 --> 00:42:52.529
He's in his room.

848
00:43:00.161 --> 00:43:02.872
[rock music playing
through headphones]

849
00:43:04.332 --> 00:43:05.874
Hey! Hey!

850
00:43:05.875 --> 00:43:07.752
Take those fuckin' things off.

851
00:43:08.962 --> 00:43:10.587
-What the hell do you want?
-What are you doing

852
00:43:10.588 --> 00:43:12.339
hanging around with Sweeney?
You shouldn't be doing that.

853
00:43:12.340 --> 00:43:13.674
What. does that
make you nervous?

854
00:43:13.675 --> 00:43:15.515
I understand he told you
to stay away from him.

855
00:43:17.637 --> 00:43:19.179
You honestly expect me
to believe that bullshit

856
00:43:19.180 --> 00:43:21.056
you were spilling the other day?

857
00:43:21.057 --> 00:43:23.225
About how some Puerto Rican guy
who killed Pat Murphy?

858
00:43:23.226 --> 00:43:24.518
Oh. he magically gets killed

859
00:43:24.519 --> 00:43:25.602
after you beat
the shit out of me!

860
00:43:25.603 --> 00:43:27.146
Oh. what? You think

861
00:43:27.147 --> 00:43:28.772
-Sweeney and I killed Pat?
-Who cares?

862
00:43:28.773 --> 00:43:30.984
-I just want my job back!
-You're playin' with fire!

863
00:43:32.193 --> 00:43:33.360
I'm tryin' to protect you!

864
00:43:33.361 --> 00:43:34.737
I can take care of myself!

865
00:43:34.738 --> 00:43:36.905
No. you can't!
In fact. I know you can't!

866
00:43:36.906 --> 00:43:38.741
Leave me alone. and stay
the fuck out of my life!

867
00:43:38.742 --> 00:43:40.617
Yeah. okay.

868
00:43:40.618 --> 00:43:41.911
All right. tough guy.

869
00:43:45.081 --> 00:43:46.332
What's this?

870
00:43:46.333 --> 00:43:47.958
Hmm?

871
00:43:47.959 --> 00:43:49.126
What. are you selling this shit?

872
00:43:49.127 --> 00:43:50.502
Or you just using it?

873
00:43:50.503 --> 00:43:52.921
What the fuck are you doing?
That's not mine!

874
00:43:52.922 --> 00:43:54.174
You know what?

875
00:43:56.051 --> 00:43:58.510
One day. you're gonna
thank me for this.

876
00:43:58.511 --> 00:43:59.928
Fuck you!

877
00:43:59.929 --> 00:44:02.599
[tense music]

878
00:44:27.248 --> 00:44:28.540
Any chatter?

879
00:44:28.541 --> 00:44:29.709
Not yet.

880
00:44:36.841 --> 00:44:38.467
I want you to meet the others.

881
00:44:38.468 --> 00:44:39.552
Mary!

882
00:44:43.306 --> 00:44:46.558
Now. you've all heard
of the girl in the grey coat.

883
00:44:46.559 --> 00:44:48.352
Now you're lookin' at her.

884
00:44:48.353 --> 00:44:50.104
This is Sarah McKenna.

885
00:44:50.105 --> 00:44:52.481
AKA Bridget Walsh.

886
00:44:52.482 --> 00:44:54.817
This is
Tadhg McKenna's daughter.

887
00:44:54.818 --> 00:44:56.652
Now. she's currently called
Bridget Walsh because of

888
00:44:56.653 --> 00:44:59.113
the Interpol warrant
that bears her name

889
00:44:59.114 --> 00:45:00.657
for the bombings
of the London Tube.

890
00:45:01.783 --> 00:45:03.201
She's a hero.

891
00:45:04.661 --> 00:45:07.121
This here's Logan.
you'll remember him.

892
00:45:07.122 --> 00:45:09.957
He's a history teacher from
Boston. long-time sympathizer.

893
00:45:09.958 --> 00:45:11.333
I have family in Belfast.

894
00:45:11.334 --> 00:45:13.085
It's an honor to meet you.

895
00:45:13.086 --> 00:45:14.878
And that's Donal.
who you've met.

896
00:45:14.879 --> 00:45:17.256
He's from Derry.
He came over with me.

897
00:45:17.257 --> 00:45:19.800
He's an explosive expert. apparently.

898
00:45:19.801 --> 00:45:21.427
Careful there. Donal.

899
00:45:21.428 --> 00:45:24.430
As long as nobody sneezes.
I'm all right.

900
00:45:24.431 --> 00:45:25.598
Cheers. Bridget.

901
00:45:26.558 --> 00:45:28.934
That's Mary.
She's from Hell's Kitchen.

902
00:45:28.935 --> 00:45:31.145
I've seen you speak at NORAID.

903
00:45:31.146 --> 00:45:32.522
Is she joining us?

904
00:45:33.481 --> 00:45:35.941
To Mary's point...

905
00:45:35.942 --> 00:45:37.568
they've all taken the oath

906
00:45:37.569 --> 00:45:39.903
of loyalty
to the Irish Republican Army.

907
00:45:39.904 --> 00:45:41.322
Any objections?

908
00:45:43.158 --> 00:45:44.742
The loyalty oath.

909
00:45:47.078 --> 00:45:48.496
Yeah. I know it well.

910
00:45:49.914 --> 00:45:52.166
Do you have a gun
and a Bible handy?

911
00:45:52.167 --> 00:45:53.585
Yeah. we do.

912
00:45:58.381 --> 00:46:00.924
[tense music]

913
00:46:00.925 --> 00:46:02.260
[officer]
Come on. Let's go.

914
00:46:03.261 --> 00:46:04.679
Move.

915
00:46:08.391 --> 00:46:09.684
Watch your head.

916
00:46:14.522 --> 00:46:16.399
-Appreciate it.
-[car door shutting]

917
00:46:20.195 --> 00:46:23.615
Moira. don't worry.
It's what's best for the boy.

918
00:46:27.785 --> 00:46:29.245
Guess she's not a fan of yours.

919
00:46:46.012 --> 00:46:47.931
-[applause]
-Thank you.

920
00:46:50.266 --> 00:46:51.850
This is very humbling.

921
00:46:51.851 --> 00:46:53.019
Wow. 1980.

922
00:46:54.395 --> 00:46:55.563
Time flies.

923
00:46:57.065 --> 00:46:58.607
Especially you get to be my age.

924
00:46:58.608 --> 00:47:00.985
[crowd laughing]

925
00:47:02.654 --> 00:47:03.696
[clears throat]

926
00:47:05.990 --> 00:47:08.283
My father left me two things...

927
00:47:08.284 --> 00:47:10.619
that are very important to me.

928
00:47:10.620 --> 00:47:12.371
His rosary...

929
00:47:12.372 --> 00:47:14.039
and a debt

930
00:47:14.040 --> 00:47:16.375
that I never got to repay...

931
00:47:16.376 --> 00:47:17.794
until tonight.

932
00:47:18.920 --> 00:47:21.088
That debt was not money.

933
00:47:21.089 --> 00:47:23.298
It was the price of keepin'
our name outta the gutter

934
00:47:23.299 --> 00:47:25.300
and our heads above the water.

935
00:47:25.301 --> 00:47:28.011
I. Sarah McKenna.

936
00:47:28.012 --> 00:47:30.222
AKA Bridget Walsh.

937
00:47:30.223 --> 00:47:31.723
do solemnly swear

938
00:47:31.724 --> 00:47:33.183
in the presence of Almighty God

939
00:47:33.184 --> 00:47:34.476
and my comrades in arms

940
00:47:34.477 --> 00:47:36.603
to uphold and protect

941
00:47:36.604 --> 00:47:38.063
the Irish Republican Army

942
00:47:38.064 --> 00:47:41.275
with all that I have
and all I may ever be.

943
00:47:41.276 --> 00:47:43.360
[Sweeney]
It's been paid by bricklayers

944
00:47:43.361 --> 00:47:45.320
who drank their pain.

945
00:47:45.321 --> 00:47:47.781
by proud Irish mothers

946
00:47:47.782 --> 00:47:49.616
who scrubbed
other people's floors

947
00:47:49.617 --> 00:47:52.202
so their sons wouldn't
have to steal.

948
00:47:52.203 --> 00:47:55.497
It's been paid
in favors and funerals.

949
00:47:55.498 --> 00:47:57.833
In silence...

950
00:47:57.834 --> 00:48:00.002
and in fists.

951
00:48:00.003 --> 00:48:01.838
In blood we never bragged about.

952
00:48:03.381 --> 00:48:04.882
We built this neighborhood.

953
00:48:06.301 --> 00:48:08.468
And. yeah. we bled for it.

954
00:48:08.469 --> 00:48:11.096
And we buried
more than a few good souls

955
00:48:11.097 --> 00:48:13.515
to make sure we hold onto it.

956
00:48:13.516 --> 00:48:16.893
I pledge obedience
without question

957
00:48:16.894 --> 00:48:18.562
to follow commands.

958
00:48:18.563 --> 00:48:20.606
to carry out justice.

959
00:48:20.607 --> 00:48:22.316
to keep the secrets
of this cause

960
00:48:22.317 --> 00:48:24.568
until my last breath

961
00:48:24.569 --> 00:48:27.195
or until Ireland stands whole.

962
00:48:27.196 --> 00:48:28.739
[Sweeney]
And we did it with pride

963
00:48:28.740 --> 00:48:30.950
because we belong.

964
00:48:31.618 --> 00:48:33.660
Tonight. we remember who we are.

965
00:48:33.661 --> 00:48:35.662
And who we will never be.

966
00:48:35.663 --> 00:48:37.539
We're not some
forgotten little tribe

967
00:48:37.540 --> 00:48:39.499
in a tiny corner of Manhattan.

968
00:48:39.500 --> 00:48:42.085
We Irish are its spine.

969
00:48:42.086 --> 00:48:44.713
[Bridget]
I swear to fight. to suffer.

970
00:48:44.714 --> 00:48:46.924
and. if called. to die...

971
00:48:48.301 --> 00:48:51.261
for the dream
of a United Ireland.

972
00:48:51.262 --> 00:48:53.013
Until the tricolor
flies in peace

973
00:48:53.014 --> 00:48:55.766
from Belfast to Derry.
or I lie beneath it.

974
00:48:55.767 --> 00:48:57.184
So help me God.

975
00:48:57.185 --> 00:48:59.227
[Sweeney]
When I say thank you tonight.

976
00:48:59.228 --> 00:49:01.980
I'm talking not only
about this lovely award.

977
00:49:01.981 --> 00:49:03.440
[speaking Gaelic]

978
00:49:03.441 --> 00:49:05.359
[Sweeney]
I'm talking about a legacy.

979
00:49:05.360 --> 00:49:07.944
The kind you don't hang
on the wall.

980
00:49:07.945 --> 00:49:10.073
a legacy you carry
in your heart.

981
00:49:12.200 --> 00:49:14.493
It's in your bones.

982
00:49:14.494 --> 00:49:16.912
And I promise you
right here and now.

983
00:49:16.913 --> 00:49:19.665
long as I'm breathing.

984
00:49:19.666 --> 00:49:21.291
nobody is gonna forget that

985
00:49:21.292 --> 00:49:24.169
we Irish built
this neighborhood!

986
00:49:24.170 --> 00:49:26.923
[cheering]

987
00:49:36.182 --> 00:49:38.225
[♪ House of the Rising Sun ♪
[playing]

988
00:49:38.226 --> 00:49:41.269
<i>♪ I got one foot ♪</i>

989
00:49:41.270 --> 00:49:44.774
<i>♪ On the platform ♪</i>

990
00:49:48.444 --> 00:49:52.072
<i>♪ And another one ♪</i>

991
00:49:52.073 --> 00:49:56.452
<i>♪ On the train ♪</i>

992
00:49:58.371 --> 00:50:03.208
<i>♪ I'm going home ♪</i>

993
00:50:03.209 --> 00:50:08.630
<i>♪ To New Orleans ♪</i>

994
00:50:08.631 --> 00:50:11.133
<i>♪ To wear ♪</i>

995
00:50:11.134 --> 00:50:15.179
<i>♪ That ball and chain ♪</i>

996
00:50:16.889 --> 00:50:18.933
[gurgling]

997
00:50:24.480 --> 00:50:25.814
Looks like the Italians
weren't too happy

998
00:50:25.815 --> 00:50:27.274
with you selling that coke.

999
00:50:27.275 --> 00:50:28.901
[chuckles]

1000
00:50:33.239 --> 00:50:34.574
Yeah.

1001
00:50:37.285 --> 00:50:38.493
You wanna get a beer?

1002
00:50:38.494 --> 00:50:43.039
<i>♪ And it's been the ruin ♪</i>

1003
00:50:43.040 --> 00:50:48.796
<i>♪ Of many a poor boy ♪</i>

1004
00:50:50.381 --> 00:50:53.633
<i>♪ And God ♪</i>

1005
00:50:53.634 --> 00:50:56.512
<i>♪ I know ♪</i>

1006
00:50:57.847 --> 00:51:02.727
<i>♪ I'm one ♪</i>

1007
00:51:06.189 --> 00:51:10.067
[♪ House of the Rising Sun ♪
[continues]

1008
00:51:55.822 --> 00:51:58.157
Subtitling: difuze

1009
00:52:08.751 --> 00:52:12.922
[police siren]

1009
